Description: Skip nondeterministic wall-clock benchmarks on Launchpad builders
 The maximum-density, long-snake, and mature-ecosystem benchmarks remain
 enabled upstream and in controlled CI.
 Shared PPA builders have produced materially different timings for identical
 source, so failing the package build on their wall-clock result is unreliable.
Author: Matthew Stanton <stantonmatthewj@gmail.com>
Origin: upstream
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-08-26
--- a/tests/qml/tst_snakes.qml
+++ b/tests/qml/tst_snakes.qml
@@ -1771,4 +1771,6 @@ TestCase {
     function test_maxDensitySimulationHasRealtimeHeadroom() {
+        skip("Wall-clock performance is validated in controlled upstream CI")
+
         visualContext.animationDensity = 100
         visualContext.trailAmount = 100
         visualContext.snakeIntelligence = 100
@@ -1805,4 +1807,6 @@ TestCase {
     function test_longSnakeSimulationHasRealtimeHeadroom() {
+        skip("Wall-clock performance is validated in controlled upstream CI")
+
         visualContext.snakeDeadlyWalls = false
         visual.snakes = [visual.makeSnake(0)]
         const snake = visual.snakes[0]
@@ -1824,4 +1828,6 @@ TestCase {
     function test_matureEcosystemHasRealtimeHeadroom() {
+        skip("Wall-clock performance is validated in controlled upstream CI")
+
         visualContext.animationDensity = 55
         visualContext.trailAmount = 100
         visualContext.snakeIntelligence = 100
